WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.835
Communication and documentation run through the entire incident response lifecycle.

00:00:04.835 --> 00:00:08.700
They are how teams keep technical work, business decisions, and accountability aligned.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.830
Useful records include timelines, evidence references, affected assets, owners,

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.245
decisions made, approvals, actions taken,

00:00:15.245 --> 00:00:17.115
open questions, and known assumptions.

00:00:17.115 --> 00:00:19.000
Different audiences need different detail.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.840
Analysts may need log references and hypotheses.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.930
Executives may need impact, risk, and next decisions.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:29.020
Legal and privacy teams may need data categories, notification considerations,

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:30.300
and preservation status.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:33.150
System owners need practical recovery and validation steps.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.560
Good communication is clear about uncertainty.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.200
It should not overstate what the team knows, and it should not hide material risk.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.960
Lessons learned are the bridge from response to improvement.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:45.400
A post-incident review should identify what worked, what slowed the team down,

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.400
which detections or logs were missing,

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.190
whether access or backups behaved as expected, and what playbooks need updates.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:52.246
The goal is not blame.

00:00:52.246 --> 00:00:55.110
The goal is a concrete improvement plan with owners, deadlines,

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:57.940
and evidence that the organization will be better prepared next

00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:58.190
time.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.900
Documentation should be written as the response unfolds,

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.808
not reconstructed entirely afterward.

00:01:02.808 --> 00:01:05.490
Time stamps, decision owners, evidence locations,

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:08.080
and open questions are much easier to capture in the moment.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.315
Clear notes also protect the team from confusion when shifts change,

00:01:11.315 --> 00:01:12.520
leaders ask for updates,

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.440
or a later review examines why a decision was made.
